@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

### AI: ask (public while testing)
POST {{baseUrl}}/ai/ask
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "prompt": "Explain a reverse proxy in one sentence"
}

### Auth: sign up (email must be new each time; also signs you in)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/sign-up
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Test",
  "lastName": "User",
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "password": "12345678"
}

### Auth: sign in
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/sign-in
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "password": "12345678"
}

### Auth: who am I? (needs a session cookie from sign-up or sign-in)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me

### Auth: sign out
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/sign-out

### Photo: create demo user + photo + metadata + album (needs sign-in: global guard)
POST {{baseUrl}}/photo/demo

### Photo: list photos with relations (needs sign-in)
GET {{baseUrl}}/photo

### AI: stream the answer over SSE (chunks arrive as events)
GET {{baseUrl}}/ai/stream?prompt=Explain%20a%20reverse%20proxy%20in%20three%20sentences

### Photo: upload an image (needs sign-in; put a JPEG/PNG next to this file as sample.jpg)
POST {{baseUrl}}/photo
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----form

------form
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="name"

Me and Bears
------form
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="sample.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./sample.jpg
------form--

### Photo: re-run the AI description for photo 1 (uses the stored file)
POST {{baseUrl}}/photo/1/describe

### Photo: download the stored image
GET {{baseUrl}}/photo/1/file

### Chat: the model calls tools to read YOUR photos (needs sign-in)
POST {{baseUrl}}/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "What photos have I uploaded, and what are they about?"
}

### Photo: search by meaning (needs sign-in and photos that were described)
GET {{baseUrl}}/photo/search?q=official%20paperwork
